E('public','/ˈpʌblɪk/','公共的；公众的；公开的；公众〔the public〕','从私人小圈子打开到社会大众：大家能用、大家有关，或大家能知道。','来自法语 public 和拉丁 publicus，后者较早形式 poplicus 接 populus 民众。',PUBLIC+[['英语 public〔名词〕','形容词名词化，常在 the public 中表示公众']],'public transport 是公共交通，public opinion 是公众意见，make something public 是把事情公开。the public 是公众这一群体，不是某一个公共场所。','public services；public opinion；make public；open to the public。','private 限于个人或特定圈子；public 面向大众。public 不自动等于免费，公共交通也可以收费。',('The garden is open to the public on weekends.','花园周末向公众开放。'),('They decided to make the survey results public.','他们决定公开调查结果。'),('Reliable public transport makes the town easier to live in.','可靠的公共交通让这座城镇更宜居。'),sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/public','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/public_1','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/public_2']),
